cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Same Code, Same Input, Different Answer: code and analysis for a chaotic N-body reproducibility test"
abstract: "A small open N-body experiment (500 equal-mass stars, Plummer sphere) showing that trajectories diverge exponentially under rounding-level changes while the cluster's overall statistics stay within natural variability, so open code alone does not make a chaotic simulation reproducible."
